Problem Context: Auditorium Seat Booking

Aim To implement a C++ program using dynamic constructors and destructors to allocate and release memory for a two-dimensional auditorium seat map. To understand object creation, destruction, dynamic memory allocation and Resource Acquisition Is Initialization (RAII).
Theory A dynamic constructor allocates memory dynamically during object creation using the new operator.
A destructor is a special member function that is automatically called when an object is destroyed. It releases dynamically allocated memory using delete or delete[].

RAII (Resource Acquisition Is Initialization) is a programming technique in which resources are acquired during object construction and released automatically during object destruction. 3. Algorithm

Start the program.
Create a class named Auditorium.
Declare rows, seats and a two-dimensional seat map.
Allocate memory dynamically using new.
Initialize all seats as available.
Implement a function to book a seat.
