Alternative Concept and Complexity Analysis The seat map can also be implemented using a single continuous memory block or a vector of vectors.
Alternative 1: Single Block Allocation char* seatMap = new char[rows * seats];

// Access seat using: seatMap[r * seats + s] = 'X';

delete[] seatMap;

Alternative 2: Vector of Vectors #include

vector<vector> seatMap( rows, vector(seats, 'O') );

Comparison: Feature Row Pointer Array Single Block Vector of Vectors Allocations rows + 1 1 Typically rows + 1 Access time O(1) O(1) O(1) Extra row pointers Yes No Managed internally Memory management Manual Manual Automatic

The single-block approach uses fewer allocations and improves memory locality. Vector of vectors provides automatic memory management. 12. Result Thus, the auditorium seat-booking system was implemented successfully using dynamic memory allocation, constructors and destructors. Seat booking, cancellation, object lifetime and memory release were demonstrated.
